-- statement:
--   This block sets up a log-Kodaira-dimension framework over the complex numbers. A SmoothProjectiveVariety is an integral scheme X with a structure morphism to Spec ℂ that is smooth of a stated relative dimension n and admits a closed immersion into some complex projective space compatible with the structure maps. ℂ acts on sections over any open set and on the function field. The rational canonical space is the n-th exterior power of the Kähler differentials of the function field over ℂ, and rational m-pluriforms are the m-fold tensor power of that space over the function field. On an affine open U, the regular pluriform lattice is the Γ(U)-span of the m-fold tensors of wedge products of differentials d a of regular functions. A Cartier ideal is an ideal sheaf locally generated by a single nonzero function. A ReducedSNCBoundary is a finite family of Cartier ideal sheaves whose product is Cartier and such that, for every nonempty subfamily S, the common zero locus is either empty or smooth of dimension n minus |S| (with |S| ≤ n), giving a reduced simple normal crossings divisor E, with ideal the product and support its zero set. A rational m-pluriform s is log-pluriform if, on every affine open where the product ideal is generated by t, the form t^m·s lies in the regular lattice; these form a complex subspace, the log sections. HasImageDimensionAtLeast(k) holds if for some m>0 there is a nonzero log m-pluriform s and k algebraically independent rational functions r_i over ℂ with every r_i·s also a log section, and the log Kodaira dimension is the supremum of such k in WithBot ℕ∞ (bottom when none exist). A ComplexPoint is a section of the structure map, with underlying scheme point, and the complement of E is the open complement of its support. A BoundaryFibration from (X,E) to (Y,D) is a surjective morphism over ℂ with connected fibers over every complex point of Y and with the preimage of the support of D contained in the support of E. A StratumSmoothFibration additionally requires smoothness over the complement of D, both on X and on every stratum of E. A FiberModel over a complex point y is a smooth projective variety realized as the pullback fiber, with its own reduced SNC boundary whose ideal is the pullback of E's ideal. Finally, VeryGenerally P means P holds at all complex points whose underlying points avoid some countable family of proper closed subsets of Y.
